      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "First project parser step that materializes mapped-slice header state from attacker-controlled bytes. The later embedded-reference MD5 path proves this header provided a nonnegative `ref_seq_id`; the following steps then materialize the span, embedded-reference selector, and MD5 from the same buffer."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_embedded_ref_span_must_fit_block",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "cram/cram_decode.c",
      "function": "cram_decode_slice",
      "line": 2214,
      "operands": [
        "s->hdr->ref_seq_span",
        "b->uncomp_size"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "s->hdr->ref_seq_span",
        "right": "b->uncomp_size"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_embedded_ref_span_must_fit_block",
      "fine_trace_step": 10,
      "description": "Root cause. After `s->ref_start` and `s->ref_end` are derived from the same attacker-controlled header, this guard compares `ref_seq_span - 1` against `b->uncomp_size`. A span exactly one byte larger than the embedded-reference block therefore passes. The fix changes this check to `s->hdr->ref_seq_span > b->uncomp_size`."
    },
    {
